# File And Folder Naming Rules

Use the naming style already established in this template.

## Folders

- Segment folders use kebab-case or established architecture names:
  - `modules/users/model/queries`
  - `modules/users/model/mutations`
  - `modules/users/model/stores`
  - `modules/users/ui/table`
  - `modules/users/ui/form`
  - `modules/users/ui/states`
  - `entities/user/model`
  - `shared/lib/client`
- Do not create per-hook folders like `use-user/useUser.ts`.
- Do not use `smart`, `dumb`, `containers`, `components` or `widgets` as
  default folders inside module `ui/`.

## Components

- React component files use PascalCase:
  - `UserProfile.tsx`
  - `UserAvatar.tsx`
  - `UserCard.tsx`
- Exported component identifiers also use PascalCase.
- Stories follow the component file name:
  - `UserAvatar.stories.tsx`
- In large module `ui/` folders, group components by responsibility zones:
  - `table`
  - `form`
  - `dialog`
  - `sheet`
  - `drawer`
  - `filters`
  - `states`
  - `content`
  - `toolbar`
  - `parts`
- Keep the main scenario component at the top level of `ui/` when useful for
  discoverability.

## Hooks

- Hook files use kebab-case and start with `use-`:
  - `use-update-user.ts`
  - `use-user-permissions.ts`
  - `use-url-filter.ts`
- Exported hook identifiers use camelCase and start with `use`:
  - `useUpdateUser`
  - `useUserPermissions`
  - `useUrlFilter`
- Query hooks live in `model/queries`.
- Mutation hooks live in `model/mutations`.
- Generate query hooks with `pnpm g:query`.
- Generate mutation hooks with `pnpm g:mutation`.
- Generic shared hooks live in `shared/hooks`.

## Model Files

- Query keys: `*.keys.ts`, usually inside `model/queries`.
- Zustand stores: `*.store.ts`, inside `model/stores`.
- Messages: `*.messages.ts`.
- Mappers: `*.mapper.ts`, inside `model/mappers` when needed.
- Constants: `*.constants.ts`.
- Schemas: `*.schema.ts`.

## Tests

- Tests are colocated in a `__tests__` folder next to the code being tested.
- Test files use `.test.ts` or `.test.tsx`.
- Keep the tested file name in the test name:
  - `use-update-user.test.ts`
  - `UserAvatar.test.tsx`
